# Typography

Primary UI font is **Nunito**. Dynamic numbers use the **platform system** font. Never hardcode `fontFamily: 'Nunito'` inline.

## Tokens

Import from [`lib/core/ui/theme/app.typography.dart`](lib/core/ui/theme/app.typography.dart):

- `AppTypography.boldStyle` — Nunito Bold (`FontWeight.w700`) for headers, selected labels, CTAs
- `AppTypography.semiBoldStyle` — Nunito SemiBold (`FontWeight.w600`) for body labels, nav, cards
- `AppTypography.numericStyle` — system sans + `FontFeature.tabularFigures()` for `%`, counters, timers, math digits

Assets: `assets/fonts/Nunito-Variable.ttf` registered as family `Nunito` at weights 600 and 700 in `pubspec.yaml`.

## Where to use what

| Content | Token |
| --- | --- |
| Screen / section titles, buttons, nav items, list labels | `boldStyle` or `semiBoldStyle` |
| Volume `%`, age chips, parent-gate equation / answers, timers | `numericStyle` |

```dart
// BAD — system default or inline family
Text('Music', style: TextStyle(fontWeight: FontWeight.w800));
Text('45%', style: AppTypography.boldStyle());

// GOOD
Text('Music', style: AppTypography.boldStyle(fontSize: context.rs(22)));
Text('45%', style: AppTypography.numericStyle(fontSize: context.rs(14)));
```

Cupertino theme text styles already default to Nunito via `AppTheme.data()`. Explicit styles still use `AppTypography`.
